{"availability":"available","full":"mnh-jansson/open-battery-information","name":"open-battery-information","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":1789,"forks":271,"created":"2024-05-06T10:37:55Z","updated":"2026-09-30T16:41:55Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://openbatteryinformation.github.io/","topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.925Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.925Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.925Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:37:36.518Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:27.128Z","stars":1789,"forks":271},{"at":"2026-10-04T06:51:30.925Z","stars":1789,"forks":271}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project aims to provide tools and information about various batteries in order to aid repair. It is very common for manufacturers to lock the BMS when a fault is detected to protect the device and the user. Very important feature! So when is it a problem? Well, there is always a chance for false triggering of this protection, or the fault could have been temporary or even repaired. In this case it would be wasteful to throw out a perfectly good BMS just because its software says it is faulty.","The desktop application is deprecated. The old desktop application (Python/Tkinter) has been removed from this repository and is no longer maintained. The latest version of the Python application can be found in the v0.2.3 tag. It has been replaced by a new web-based UI that runs in your browser: - Web UI / OBI-1 tool: - Live site: The web UI connects to the Arduino over Web Serial and can even flash the firmware directly from your browser, so no Python installation is needed anymore. This repository now only hosts the Arduino firmware (see ArduinoOBI/)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mnh-jansson/open-battery-information/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"